    "collapsible_content_Tiz8h4": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_Lb98Pc": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What's the difference between MoonShade and MoonShade XL?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade XL is 12ft × 9ft — 70% more coverage than the original 9ft × 7ft. XL, requires about 12 feet of mounting span, and is designed for full-size vans, motorhomes, and larger trucks. The original is sized for SUVs, crossovers, mid-size trucks, Jeeps, and smaller trailers.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Bqa4FW": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What vehicles is MoonShade XL compatible with?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade XL is built for full-size vans, RVs, and motorhomes. Moon-confirmed vehicles include the Mercedes-Benz Sprinter, Ford Transit, Ram ProMaster, Chevy Express, Winnebago Solis and Ekko, and Scamp 16. Customers have also confirmed it on the GMC Savana, Airstream Interstate and Atlas, Winnebago Travato and Revel, Storyteller MODE, and various Class A and C motorhomes. See the <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">full list</a> here.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_R4CwQi": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade XL need a roof rack?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. MoonShade XL uses MoonMounts or semi-permanent anchors — no roof rack, no drilling.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_pRwz3i": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How much does MoonShade XL weigh?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>12.6 lbs. Packs into a bag — designed to store inside the van when not in use.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_KpaWJd": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade XL hold up in wind?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. Customers have confirmed it at 30-40 mph. For exposed conditions, guy lines add meaningful stability.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Qjwtza": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can MoonShade XL cover both the side door and rear door on a van?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes — depending on how you position it, XL can cover the side door, rear door, or both in a two-MoonShade setup.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_WGRH4c": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MoonShade waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We don’t “waterproof” our fabric because it would degrade the integrity of its UV resistance over time. That said, it is seam-sealed and the fabric is a technical 420 ripstop that sheds water like an umbrella.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
